[2026-01-30T16:24:12.812Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EARfJuUrBrHMy4yYtT7Wmp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation: Implement interactive Sankey and causal chain editor with drag-and-drop flow building and what-if analysis\n     2→\n     3→## Context Area\n     4→Timeline & Flow Visualizations\n     5→\n     6→## Description\n     7→Implement interactive Sankey and causal chain editor with drag-and-drop flow building and what-if analysis\n     8→\n     9→## Implementation Details\n    10→\n    11→## Interactive Causal Flow Editor with What-If Analysis\n    12→\n    13→### Vision\n    14→Transform the static causal flow visualization into an interactive editor where users can explore, modify, and test causal relationships. Add Sankey diagram support for flow magnitude visualization and enable what-if analysis by adjusting chain parameters.\n    15→\n    16→### Business Value\n    17→- Critical for scenario planning and risk assessment\n    18→- Enables active exploration vs passive viewing\n    19→- What-if analysis supports decision-making\n    20→- Sankey diagrams show relative importance of flows\n    21→- Interactive editing creates engagement\n    22→\n    23→### Scope\n    24→**Included:**\n    25→- Sankey diagram mode showing flow magnitudes\n    26→- Drag-and-drop causal chain editing\n    27→- Add/remove/reorder chain steps\n    28→- What-if sliders to adjust step weights\n    29→- Impact propagation visualization\n    30→- Alternative path highlighting\n    31→- Chain comparison (compare two scenarios)\n    32→- Export chain as shareable diagram\n    33→- Automatic layout optimization\n    34→- Confidence visualization on edges\n    35→\n    36→**Out of Scope:**\n    37→- Full process modeling (BPMN-level)\n    38→- Quantitative simulation\n    39→\n    40→### Key Components\n    41→1. **SankeyDiagram** - Flow magnitude visualization\n    42→2. **EditableCausalChain** - Interactive chain with drag-and-drop\n    43→3. **ChainStepEditor** - Modify individual step properties\n    44→4. **WhatIfControls** - Parameter adjustment sliders\n    45→5. **ImpactPropagation** - Visual ripple effect for changes\n    46→6. **AlternativePathHighlighter** - Show branching possibilities\n    47→7. **ChainComparator** - Side-by-side scenario comparison\n    48→8. **AutoLayoutEngine** - Optimize node positions\n    49→9. **ChainExporter** - Export as image or JSON\n    50→\n    51→### Technical Approach\n    52→- D3-sankey for Sankey diagram layout\n    53→- @dnd-kit for drag-and-drop editing\n    54→- React Flow or custom SVG for chain visualization\n    55→- Dagre or ELK for automatic layout\n    56→- Optimistic UI updates during editing\n    57→- URL state for shareable configurations\n    58→- Canvas export via html2canvas\n    59→\n    60→### Files to Create/Modify\n    61→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/SankeyDiagram.tsx`\n    62→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/EditableCausalChain.tsx`\n    63→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ChainStepEditor.tsx`\n    64→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/WhatIfControls.tsx`\n    65→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ImpactPropagation.tsx`\n    66→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ChainComparator.tsx`\n    67→- Create: `src/lib/causalLayout.ts`\n    68→- Create: `src/hooks/useCausalEditor.ts`\n    69→- Modify: CausalFlow.tsx - Integrate editable mode\n    70→\n    71→### Success Criteria\n    72→- Sankey diagram accurately shows flow magnitudes\n    73→- Drag-and-drop reordering works smoothly\n    74→- What-if changes propagate visually\n    75→- Layout stays clean during editing\n    76→- Comparison mode shows differences clearly\n    77→- Export produces high-quality image\n    78→- Undo/redo works for all edits\n    79→\n    80→### Potential Challenges\n    81→- Layout stability during drag operations\n    82→- Sankey calculation for complex chains\n    83→- What-if propagation logic complexity\n    84→- Performance with many parallel chains\n    85→\n    86→## Instructions\n    87→\n    88→1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n    89→2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n    90→3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n    91→4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n    92→5. Test the changes work as expected\n    93→\n    94→## Notes\n    95→\n    96→This requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\n    97→Focus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n    98→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"81dd57fd-4106-460e-8313-5cb3869a882e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\dir-1769788096737-implement-interactive-sankey-and-causal.md","content":"# Implementation: Implement interactive Sankey and causal chain editor with drag-and-drop flow building and what-if analysis\n\n## Context Area\nTimeline & Flow Visualizations\n\n## Description\nImplement interactive Sankey and causal chain editor with drag-and-drop flow building and what-if analysis\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Interactive Causal Flow Editor with What-If Analysis\n\n### Vision\nTransform the static causal flow visualization into an interactive editor where users can explore, modify, and test causal relationships. Add Sankey diagram support for flow magnitude visualization and enable what-if analysis by adjusting chain parameters.\n\n### Business Value\n- Critical for scenario planning and risk assessment\n- Enables active exploration vs passive viewing\n- What-if analysis supports decision-making\n- Sankey diagrams show relative importance of flows\n- Interactive editing creates engagement\n\n### Scope\n**Included:**\n- Sankey diagram mode showing flow magnitudes\n- Drag-and-drop causal chain editing\n- Add/remove/reorder chain steps\n- What-if sliders to adjust step weights\n- Impact propagation visualization\n- Alternative path highlighting\n- Chain comparison (compare two scenarios)\n- Export chain as shareable diagram\n- Automatic layout optimization\n- Confidence visualization on edges\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Full process modeling (BPMN-level)\n- Quantitative simulation\n\n### Key Components\n1. **SankeyDiagram** - Flow magnitude visualization\n2. **EditableCausalChain** - Interactive chain with drag-and-drop\n3. **ChainStepEditor** - Modify individual step properties\n4. **WhatIfControls** - Parameter adjustment sliders\n5. **ImpactPropagation** - Visual ripple effect for changes\n6. **AlternativePathHighlighter** - Show branching possibilities\n7. **ChainComparator** - Side-by-side scenario comparison\n8. **AutoLayoutEngine** - Optimize node positions\n9. **ChainExporter** - Export as image or JSON\n\n### Technical Approach\n- D3-sankey for Sankey diagram layout\n- @dnd-kit for drag-and-drop editing\n- React Flow or custom SVG for chain visualization\n- Dagre or ELK for automatic layout\n- Optimistic UI updates during editing\n- URL state for shareable configurations\n- Canvas export via html2canvas\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/SankeyDiagram.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/EditableCausalChain.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ChainStepEditor.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/WhatIfControls.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ImpactPropagation.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/flow/ChainComparator.tsx`\n- Create: `src/lib/causalLayout.ts`\n- Create: `src/hooks/useCausalEditor.ts`\n- Modify: CausalFlow.tsx - Integrate editable mode\n\n### Success Criteria\n- Sankey diagram accurately shows flow magnitudes\n- Drag-and-drop reordering works smoothly\n- What-if changes propagate visually\n- Layout stays clean during editing\n- Comparison mode shows differences clearly\n- Export produces high-quality image\n- Undo/redo works for all edits\n\n### Potential Challenges\n- Layout stability during drag operations\n- Sankey calculation for complex chains\n- What-if propagation logic complexity\n- Performance with many parallel chains\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98}}}
